# Copy this file to .env. Do not commit .env.
#
# Make.com custom webhook for the scenario that creates one GroupMe per group.
# In Make, add a GroupMe "Create a group" module, then add each phone as a member.
# The webhook receives JSON: groupId, name, interest, size, phones, emails, members, description, message.
# members is a list of { nickname, phone, email }. Phone is empty when the person used email.
# In Make, iterate members. On Add a Member, map Phone to phone and Email to email.
# After every member is added, use GroupMe "Create a Message" once. Map Text to message.
# To show a join link on the site, respond with JSON: { "groupmeUrl": "https://..." }
MAKE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional. If set, Rex Connect sends it as the x-rex-secret header.
MAKE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
